From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgx-build <build@dgx-01.local>
Date: Sun, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] logits: run the multi-row vocabulary projection on b12x
 gemm.bf16_gemv

The Qwen3.8-Flash-Next verify head ([124160, 2560] BF16 per node, 636 MB)
costs 3.60 ms of a 55.03 ms c1 decode step -- 6.5% -- on cuBLAS's
cutlass_80_wmma_tensorop_bf16_s161616gemm_bf16_16x16_128x2_tn_align8, at 65%
of the LPDDR5x roofline.

It already takes the b12x route. `use_b12x_vocab_projection` is true, the head
is registered, and its plans are primed ("b12x priming
gemm.bf16_vocab_projection" in the boot log). The route is a dead end at
M > 1: b12x.gemm.bf16_vocab_projection's tuning contract admits its Triton
backend only for `max_tokens == 1` (_default_config, _validate_config and
_tuning_parameters all gate on it), so every other capacity resolves to
`backend="torch"` and `materialize` hands back
`torch.nn.functional.linear`. The saved plan cache confirms it: exactly one
gemm.bf16_vocab_projection record exists for this model, `{algorithm: row,
backend: triton, block_k: 4096, num_warps: 4}` -- the M=1 plan -- and the
torch backend compiles nothing, so no other capacity leaves a record.

The Triton kernel cannot be widened in place: its grid is (N, rows) with one
program per (vocab row, token row), so it re-reads the whole weight matrix per
token. b12x.gemm.bf16_gemv's SIMT backend is the kernel for this shape --
one CTA per output column, up to SMALL_M_MAX=8 source rows accumulated against
a single weight load, vectorised 16B global loads. This declares a GEMV plan
instead of a torch plan for every prepared capacity in 1 < M <= SMALL_M_MAX,
and dispatches to it in _apply_head.

Bit-exactness: NOT bit-identical. bf16 x bf16 products are exact in fp32 under
both kernels, but the summation order differs (cuBLAS: 16x16x16 WMMA tiles
walking K; b12x: 128-thread strided fp32 FMA chains plus a tree reduction), so
the result differs by fp32 rounding, ~5e-6 relative over K=2560. Gate with
scripts/logits_equiv.py at --tol 1e-3.

Anything the GEMV cannot serve -- M = 1 (which keeps the Triton vocabulary
GEMV), M > 8, a misaligned or non-contiguous hidden-state buffer, a
quantized head, b12x absent -- keeps the stock path and is bit-identical to
stock. VLLM_B12X_VOCAB_GEMV=0 reverts without a rebuild.

Two log lines make the routing decision greppable at boot:
  "b12x vocab projection plan: head=%dx%d capacity=%d component=%s"
  "b12x vocab projection: rows=%d component=%s"

Applies on top of 8e1f1e587f.
